※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4491

※ An array holds values of one type, so an array made out of two others holds
※ what both of them held.  Where the two held different things there is no
※ such type, and which of the two the answer would be is not something to
※ guess at.

let a: u8⟦3⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8⟧
let w: u16⟦2⟧ = ⟦4u16, 5u16⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let both: u16⟦5⟧ = a ⧺ w
    0u8
